body:
It might be worth checking whether this works with `ghs_` tokens: https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/fa812ef2b1ab1240ca023b7a4b720cbeef7fbdcd/internal/attachments/client.go#L91-L109

I'm not sure that `ghs_` tokens don't have a viewer, so `viewerPermission` might be `null` and so they won't pass the `WRITE` check. Introspection query:

```gql
gh api graphql -f query='
query {
  __type(name: "Repository") {
    fields {
      name
      description
    }
  }
}' --jq '.data.__type.fields[] | select(.name == "viewerPermission")'
```

Shows this information:

```
{
  "description": "The users permission level on the repository. Will return null if authenticated as an GitHub App.",
  "name": "viewerPermission"
}
```

All in all, I'm not sure that it makes sense to have this kind of client side check either, and it's probably better to just the server address this kind of issue, but @BagToad may have had his reasons for adding it. A simple and unintrusive change would be to only do the viewer check if we're not dealing with a `ghs_` token.
